 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Sydney CBD's Friday gap is now about **0.78**, compared with about **0.88** before COVID. Fridays are relatively quieter than they were.\n\n- **Pre-COVID baseline (Jan–Feb 2020):** about 0.88 on average. The monthly figures were 0.84 in January and 0.92 in February, and the tool's baseline window is 6 Jan to 6 Mar 2020.\n- **Latest (September 2026):** 0.78. The April–September 2026 average is about 0.79.\n\nSo the ratio is roughly 0.10 lower than pre-COVID, which means Friday 3–7pm tap-ons are running at about 78% of the Tuesday–Thursday average, down from about 88%. The gap has been fairly flat since 2023, mostly between 0.76 and 0.80. Every month since mid-2022 has been below the pre-COVID range, which was roughly 0.84–0.92.",
